# Run CSGClaw with Make

When starting or restarting the CSGClaw HTTP server / IM UI, use the **repository root** and this Makefile target:

```bash
cd /path/to/csgclaw
export CGO_ENABLED=1
make run
```

- **`make run`** runs `go run ./cmd/csgclaw serve` (see `Makefile` target `run`) after `boxlite-setup` if needed.
- **CGO must be enabled** for BoxLite (`CGO_ENABLED=1`); omitting it breaks linking or native runtime.

Other useful targets (see `make help`):

- **`make build`** — produce `bin/csgclaw` (then `./bin/csgclaw serve` if you prefer not to use `go run`).
- **`make onboard`** — bootstrap `~/.csgclaw/config.toml` defaults when appropriate.

After startup, open the URL printed in the log (typically `http://127.0.0.1:18080/`). Do not paste real API keys or access tokens into chat; `config.toml` is the source of truth for provider URLs and keys.
